{
  "_doc": "src/shared/course.ts (tool 5 of Lote 1: the simulated test course with scoring) against contracts/courses/basic.json, a hand-written copy of CourseLayout.Default() in TestCourse.cs (the C# is the source of truth; `layout_checks` pins the layout). The simulator has no physics: a collision is a simple volume test (a sphere of `constants.droneRadius` around the position against cylinders, boxes and the tube of each ring). Frame: metres from the take-off point (north, east) and height over the ground. `volume`: hitsPylon / hitsBox / hitsRing (and the wall gap of the layout) at their borders, every case `{ name, p: [n, e, alt], out }` against `shape` (hit = true; the bounds are inclusive). `gates`: crossesGate(gate, segment prev -> now = [pn, pe, pa, n, e, alt]) = the segment starts strictly behind the ring's plane (axial < 0), ends on or past it (axial >= 0), and crosses it within `ring radius - ringTube` of the axis. `zones`: zoneContains (inclusive). `scripts`: CourseRun on synthetic samples `[dt, n, e, alt, count = 1]` (the sample repeated `count` times, courseStep each); `expect.events` are the events with the 0-based index of the sample that raised them, `after_each` the state after every row of `steps`; `resetAfter` = resetCourse() before that row. A lap waits for the take-off (the drone was at or under 0.3 m and climbs over `startAltitude` within `startRadius` of the pad) or, after a reset in the air, for the first checkpoint; the time adds dt only when 0 < dt < 1; collisions are edge-triggered per obstacle id (`pylon:i`, `wall:i`, `gate:i`); the checkpoints go in order. `laps`: `polyline_clean` flies `route` as TestCourseTests.FlyRoute does (40 take-off steps of +0.1 m, then straight legs at 6 m/s, dt 1/30 s, steps = ceil(length / (6 dt))); `polyline_two_pylons` is the same with the slalom flown through pylons 0 and 1 (exactly two collisions); `simulator` flies the route with the browser simulator (createSim(22), takeoff 3.5 m, fly_to every waypoint, dt 1/30 s, 7/7 and 0 collisions; the simulator's own numbers are pinned by flightsim.json, here times are compared within `tolerance.sim_time`). `score`: score(run) with a penalty of `penalty_s` per collision [APROBAR]. `records`: updateRecords step by step (best clean time = the fastest attempt with 0 collisions, best penalised time = the fastest time plus the penalty, 10 last attempts newest first) and parseRecords of the text kept under twinsight.course.records.v1 (anything invalid gives empty records). `ghost`: the trace of the best attempt at 10 Hz [n, e, alt, yaw] (pushGhost keeps a sample for every 0.1 s of lap time), ghostPose interpolation (yaw the short way round) and parseGhost. Times are in seconds.",
